ast year, influenced by earlier supply constraints in …","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"capex_expansion":{"title":"Expansion (RHP)","body":"During the year, the Company commenced commercial production at its newly established Fabcity, Hyderabad facility, dedicated to TopCon Solar Cell Modules, marking Surana Solar's re-entry into the solar cell module manufacturing space. The Company continues to operate its existing Cherlapally, Hyderabad manufacturing unit alongside the new Fabcity facility.","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"moat":{"title":"Strengths (RHP)","body":"- technology: Re-entry into solar cell module manufacturing with next-generation TopCon technology — evidence: commercial production commenced at the newly established Fabcity, Hyderabad facility (180 MW installed capacity) dedicated to TopCon Solar Cell Modules, described as significantly enhancing efficiency and reliability.\n- integration: In-house EPC capability alongside module manufacturing — evidence: company is 'well-equipped to deliver turnkey solar power solutions for large-scale commercial and utility projects' with proven expertise in engineering, procurement and construction.","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"risks":{"title":"Risks (RHP)","body":"- The Company has foreign currency risk on import of input materials, capital commitments, and also borrows funds in foreign currency for its business, exposing it to exchange rate fluctuations.\n- Module prices continue to remain elevated compared to the prior year, influenced by earlier supply constraints in China, affecting cost structure.\n- A portion of planned solar capacity in the sector pipeline is still pending commissioning due to regulatory and financial challenges, which can affect demand timing for the Company's products and EPC business.\n- The Company's re-entry into solar cell module manufacturing depends on the newly commissioned Fabcity TopCon facility ramping up successfully.\n- The Company transacts materially with multiple Surana/Bhagyanagar group related parties for sales, purchases and inter-company loans, creating counterparty concentration within the promoter group's broader enterprise network.\n- The Company was engaged in a dispute with Paradip Port Trust over invocation of a bank guarantee, indicating exposure to contractual/counterparty disputes in its project business.","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"strategy":{"title":"Strategies (RHP)","body":"- Widen activities by entering into EPC contracts and the solar rooftop business through participation in government and non-government tenders.\n- Re-entry into solar cell module manufacturing via the new TopCon Solar Cell Module facility to strengthen competitive positioning in the renewable energy sector.\n- Capitalize on emerging opportunities in both domestic and international markets amid growing demand for clean energy solutions.","src":"drhp","as_of":""}},"scorecard":{"symbol":"SURANASOL","fin_source":"shadow ledger (per-field legacy fallback)","fy_asof":"2026-03-31","opm_basis":"TTM 4q","opm_ttm":"-14.300000000000002","roe":"2.18","roce":"3.12","bq_a":"0","sales_cagr_3y":"-20.957458088906478","eps_cagr_3y":"-18.6500502799421","bq_b":"0","debt_equity":"0.0","interest_cover":"7.782608695652174","bq_c":"13","cfo_pat_3y":"","wc_basis":"WC/sales trend","bq_d":"0","share_cagr_3y":"-0.004064710190676557","bq_e":"6","shp_asof":"2026-06-30","promoter_pct":"45.75","promoter_prev":"44.34","pledge_basis":"pledge not in snapshot -> 0 penalty (hook)","piotroski_basis":"needs 2 FYs of BS_* -> 0 (real from FY27)","bq_f":"2","g_integrity":"5","g_execution":"0","g_capalloc":"0","g_basis":"defaults (no WTT/ledger coverage)","bq_g":"5","bq_total":"26","bq_gate":"False","stage2":"False","sector_on":"True","market_on":"True","rs_rank":"","per_a":"15","pe_ttm":"19.4519840625","pe_basis":"TTM trailing (spec band written for forward P/E)","per_b":"25","earn_accel":"ACCEL","rev_accel":"ACCEL","per_c":"25","per_d":"15","per_e":"0","per_total":"80","per_gate":"True","advt_rs":"","